.TH DANBY-SEASONALDISEASE 1
.SH NAME
danby-seasonaldisease \- SIR transmission with seasonal infectiousness
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/seasonaldisease
.SH MODEL
beta(t)=beta0(1+s cos(wt));
S'=-beta(t)SI;
I'=beta(t)SI-gamma I;
R'=gamma I.
.PP
The seasonal amplitude s remains below one so contact never becomes negative.
Changing w compares slow environmental modulation with forcing faster than the
epidemic can respond.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag any compartment bar.  Tracks set mean contact, seasonal amplitude,
frequency, and recovery.  Space pauses, period steps, r resets, and q exits.
.SH NUMERICS
The time-dependent right-hand side is tested for population conservation.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/seasonaldisease.b
.br
.B /appl/temple/seasonaldisease.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR danby-epidemic (1),
.IR populationmodel (2)
